    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CATHAY PACIFIC E\nCATHAY PACIFIC E\nLearner Chopsticks\nIf you're not eating with chopsticks you're not eating \"Chinese\". But first you've got to get the knack. These Cathay\nPacific Learner Chopsticks have a built-in \"safety\" device that lets you gain experience without losing too much weight!\nJust follow these simple instructions.\nStep 1:\nStep 2:\nGrasp one Learner Chopstick\nAdd the second Learner Chopstick\napproximately in the middle, nesting\n- holding it as you would a pencil,\nit under your thumb. Firmly press it\nbetween the tips of your thumb and\nagainst your middle finger as\nindex finger, with the shank resting\nillustrated.\nalongside the index finger.\nDISTRIBUTOR: B\u0026 J ROCKET (HONG KONG) LTD. LTD. BOX K-73500, CP OFFICE, KOWLOON, HONG KONG. BRIT. PAT. 966677, OTHER PATENTS\nStep 3:\nFirmly hold the first Chopstick\n(unmoving) in its original position\nand move the second one up and\ndown - matching the tips in a tight\npinching or holding action.\nCATHAY PACIFIC.\nStep 4:\nIf you really think you've given it a\nfair shot, and failed, turn the\nchopsticks around to the \"Western\nend\" and enjoy your meal anyway.\nCAUTION: NOT RECOMMENDED FOR SOUP.",
      "CATHAY PACIFIC E\nCATHAY PACIFIC E\nLearner\nCATHAY PACIFIC\nChopstickS Wah the Complimens of Cathy Befic"
    ],
